### Topic 33 - Employee Management API
### Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension: click "Send Request" above each request.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/employees

### 1. List all employees (3 sample employees are loaded at startup)
GET {{baseUrl}}

### 2. Filter by department (case does not matter)
GET {{baseUrl}}?department=engineering

### 3. Get one employee - notice: NO salary in the response!
GET {{baseUrl}}/1

### 4. Create an employee -> 201 Created + Location header
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Kiran",
  "lastName": "Patel",
  "email": "kiran.patel@company.com",
  "department": "Finance",
  "salary": 72000
}

### 5. Try to create the SAME email again -> 409 Conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Kiran",
  "lastName": "Again",
  "email": "kiran.patel@company.com",
  "department": "Finance",
  "salary": 50000
}

### 6. Try to sneak in "id" and "internalNotes" - both are IGNORED (they are not in the DTO)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 999,
  "firstName": "Nisha",
  "lastName": "Verma",
  "email": "nisha.verma@company.com",
  "department": "HR",
  "salary": 60000,
  "internalNotes": "trying to set HR notes"
}

### 7. Update employee 1
PUT {{baseUrl}}/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Asha",
  "lastName": "Rao",
  "email": "asha.rao@company.com",
  "department": "Architecture",
  "salary": 95000
}

### 8. Department summary (a "report" DTO)
GET {{baseUrl}}/departments/summary

### 9. Delete employee 2 -> 204 No Content
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/2

### 10. Get a missing employee -> 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/99
